.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ziv-render 1  "render " 
.SH NAME
ziv\-render \- Render one projection of an OME\-Zarr image to a single PNG or JPEG file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBziv render\fR [\fB\-\-at\fR] [\fB\-\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-region\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-quality\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISRC\fR> <\fIOUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Render one projection of an OME\-Zarr image to a single PNG or JPEG file.
.PP
The reason this earns its own command rather than "take a screenshot of `serve`": `\-\-at` takes the exact same projection identifier the server understands (for example `@z=10,c=0,overlay=nuclei:distinct:0.6`), so one call bakes a label overlay — with its palette and opacity — into a flat image. No other tool does that in one step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-at\fR \fI<AT>\fR [default: default]
Projection identifier to render, in the exact grammar `serve`\*(Aqs IIIF identifier segment understands: `default` for the image as its own metadata describes it, or a dynamic `@z=..,t=..,c=..,label=NAME[:PALETTE]` / `@...,overlay=NAME[:PALETTE[:OPACITY]]` selection
.TP
\fB\-\-size\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR [default: max]
Output size, in the same grammar as the server\*(Aqs IIIF `size` path segment: `max` (the region\*(Aqs native resolution), `w,h`, `w,` (width only), `,h` (height only), `!w,h` (fit inside, preserving aspect ratio), or `pct:N`
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR \fI<REGION>\fR [default: full]
Region to render, in the same grammar as the server\*(Aqs IIIF `region` path segment: `full`, `square`, `x,y,w,h`, or `pct:x,y,w,h`
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format: png or jpg. Inferred from <OUT>\*(Aqs extension when omitted
.TP
\fB\-\-quality\fR \fI<QUALITY>\fR
JPEG encoder quality, 0\-100 (default 85 if omitted). Applies to JPEG output only — given alongside PNG output, it is ignored, with a note rather than silently
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISRC\fR>
Store spec for the .ome.zarr image: a local filesystem path, or a remote URL (`s3://bucket/path`, `gs://bucket/path`, `az://container/path`, `http(s)://host/path`). See `serve \-\-help` for remote credential env vars
.TP
<\fIOUT\fR>
Output file to write. The format is inferred from this extension unless \-\-format overrides it
